# Shell scripts must keep LF endings: git-for-windows checkouts otherwise use
# CRLF, which breaks bash parsing (a stray CR ends up inside tokens and even
# the shebang). This is why the pre-push hook appeared "broken" on fresh
# checkouts even when its source was correct.
*.bash text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/** text eol=lf

# Rust sources and manifests: store LF, let git normalize per-platform prefs.
*.rs text
*.toml text
*.md text
*.json text
